      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To synthesize plain text to an audio byte stream, I will use the Amazon Polly service, which is a text-to-speech service that uses advanced deep learning technologies to synthesize speech that sounds like a human voice. I will import the necessary module from the boto3 library, which is the Amazon Web Services (AWS) SDK for Python. I will then create a Polly client and define a function that takes text as input, synthesizes it using the Polly service, and returns the audio stream. The provider will be identifiable by the import of the boto3 library and the use of the Polly client. </thinking>\n",
